\tag{fnip}
\taxon{Remark}
\title{The class travels with the bifurcation}
\date{2026-11-27}

\p{The class is a property of the bifurcation. Any model that
meets the same nondegeneracy and transversality conditions has
the same class, up to local topological equivalence with the
normal form. The frequency law is not part of that equivalence.
It is the smooth computation already given: near a saddle-node
on an invariant circle the period grows like the reciprocal
square root in \ref{fnip-0092}, and the frequency of an orbit
born at a Hopf point stays away from zero, as in \ref{fnip-0101}.}
